        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-neutral-100 pt-4">Which Free PDF to Excel Converter Should You Use?</h2>
        <p>If you need quick, simple conversions and don't mind the limitations, SmallPDF or Zamzar work fine. If you're already paying for Adobe Acrobat, its online converter does the job for basic documents.</p>
        <p>But if you need <strong>accurate, AI-powered extraction</strong> with the ability to verify results through confidence scoring — especially for invoices, receipts, or complex tables — <a href="/upload" class="text-brand-400 underline hover:text-brand-300">PDF2DataAI's free tier is the clear choice</a>. You get per-field confidence scores, auto-flagging of low-confidence data, and export to Excel or CSV, all without signing up.</p>
